      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I’ve made a post about this before and vrchat doesn’t want to acknowledge it as an issue but it is and I’m pretty sure I know what causes this I’m trying to find the post I made about it but they probably marked it as not a bug again \n\nWhat I believe is causing it is that your downloaded avatars and worlds are now saved locally on your device instead of their servers but even still clearing out the cache data doesn’t fix this issue also it doesn’t matter how many people are in the world you can crash for doing basically anything while you’re alone it does sound like it’s caused by a memory leak and I don’t think vrchat can do anything about it unless they move everything back to their servers and considering they had a valid reason for moving it to everyone’s local device the only thing I can see fixing this is to get a pc that can handle vrchat",
